## How sections work\
\
Every content section uses a surface modifier class:\
\
```html\
<section class="section section-cream">   <!-- cream background -->\
<section class="section section-charcoal"> <!-- dark background, light text -->\
<section class="section section-chartreuse"> <!-- chartreuse background -->\
<section class="section">                 <!-- defaults to cream -->\
```\
\
The CSS handles all text colour switching automatically when you change\
the surface class. You do not need to add colour overrides manually.\
\
---\
\
## How scroll animations work\
\
Three things are wired up via inline JavaScript at the bottom of each page:\
\
**1. Reveal on scroll**\
Add `class="reveal"` to any element. It fades up when scrolled into view.\
Stagger children with `reveal-d1` through `reveal-d6`.\
\
```html\
<h2 class="reveal">This fades in</h2>\
<p class="reveal reveal-d2">This fades in slightly later</p>\
```\
\
**2. Chartreuse highlight wipe**\
Add `class="highlight"` to any inline `<span>`. A chartreuse underline\
wipes across it when scrolled into view.\
\
```html\
<p>The system is <span class="highlight">free to use</span> after the lease.</p>\
```\
\
**3. Count-up stat counters**\
Use the `.counter` span inside a `.stat-number` span. Set the target\
number with `data-to`. For comma formatting add `data-fmt="comma"`.\
\
```html\
<span class="stat-number">\
  <span class="counter" data-to="6000" data-fmt="comma">6,000</span>\
</span>\
```\
