## Data files -- single source of truth

Two JSON files in the /data folder drive all savings figures on the site.
The website reads from data/ofgem.json only.

### Quarterly update (Ofgem price cap -- January, April, July, October)

1. Go to ofgem.gov.uk and find the new GB average unit rate (p/kWh) and
   standing charge (p/day).
2. Open data/ofgem.json and update:
   quarter, period, unit_rate_p, standing_charge_p_day,
   annual_cap_gbp, source_url, updated, next_review.
3. Do NOT change saving_10yr_gbp or saving_25yr_gbp here.
   Those come from the financial model (see below).
4. Commit and push. Cloudflare redeploys in under 60 seconds.

### Model review (saving figures -- only when model is re-run)

1. Take the residential 10-year and 25-year saving figures from the model.
2. Update data/wae-model.json: residential_saving_10yr_gbp,
   residential_saving_25yr_gbp, and the rounded _published equivalents.
3. Update data/ofgem.json: page_stats.saving_10yr_gbp and saving_25yr_gbp
   to match the rounded published figures.
4. Push once. Calculator and all pages update automatically.

Current published figures (May 2026 model):
  10-year residential saving: £8,300
  25-year residential saving: £38,000
  Baseline usage: 2,855 kWh/year

### Pages that display saving figures

calculator.html        -- reads live from data/ofgem.json via fetch()
index.html (compact)   -- reads live from data/ofgem.json via fetch()
index.html (stat bar)  -- HARDCODED: update data-to values manually
faqs.html              -- HARDCODED: search for "8,300" and "38,000"
